{"object":"A hot-swap Sun68 PCB failed after a few months despite troubleshooting, leaving the keyboard unusable when no replacement PCB could be found. The owner recommends buying a backup PCB, showing that switch hot-swap does not cover controller or PCB failure and that spare availability is part of serviceability.","predicate":"demonstrates","source_url":"http://localhost:9999/f/MechanicalKeyboards/120974/group-buy-keyboards-and-replacement-pcbs-a-lesson-learned","subject":"Sun68 owner report","text":"A Sun68 owner reports a failed hot-swap PCB after a few months, unsuccessful troubleshooting, and no available replacement, illustrating why hot-swappable switches do not make the whole board repairable without PCB spares.","title":"prop_sun68_pcb_spare_risk"}